    {
      "fileName": "silencing-strike.json",
      "id": "Yk3QGpalWDn5MhBV",
      "name": "Silencing Strike",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "Yk3QGpalWDn5MhBV",
        "folder": "GZnLEqftxPiHa5m1",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Silencing Strike",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>A quick strike to the face or mouth silences your opponent. Make a melee Strike against an enemy. If it hits, the enemy must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|against:barbarian|options:inflicts:stunned] save against your class DC.</p><hr /><p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is dazed and can barely vocalize. It's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stunned]{Stunned 1} and its speech is raspy and hard to understand. It must succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:11] to use linguistic actions or Cast a Spell, unless the spell has the subtle trait.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stunned]{Stunned 3} instead of stunned 1.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 10
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core 2"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "barbarian",
              "incapacitation",
              "rage"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 10,
